course: dictionary
lesson: 13448
title: Hostile
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hostile means unfriendly and angry, ready to argue or fight. It can also mean belonging to an enemy, or a place that is very harsh and hard to live in. Read the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «The crowd turned hostile when the match was stopped.» The clue is turned: the people changed from friendly to angry, so hostile means unfriendly and angry. Try your meaning in the sentence: "The crowd turned unfriendly and angry" still makes sense.
explain: «The soldiers came from a hostile army.» Army and soldiers are the clues. A hostile army belongs to an enemy, so the people in the story should be careful. «Antarctica is a hostile place for most animals» uses the third meaning: cold and ice make it very harsh to live in.
fact: Hostile is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a crowd, an army, or a place.
fact: Hostile means unfriendly and angry, ready to argue or fight.
fact: Hostile can mean belonging to an enemy, as in «hostile army».
fact: Hostile can describe a place or conditions that are very harsh and difficult to live in, as in «a hostile desert».
fact: Hostile to means against or opposed to something, so a word with this meaning will have to in it.
exercise: «The crowd turned hostile when the match was stopped.» What does hostile mean here? | Calm and happy | *Unfriendly and angry, ready to fight | Very quiet and shy | Lost and tired
exercise: «The soldiers came from a hostile army.» What does hostile suggest? | Very kind and friendly | Covered in snow | Hungry and tired | *Belonging to an enemy
exercise: «Antarctica is a hostile place for most animals.» What does hostile mean here? | *Very harsh and difficult to live in | Full of fun and games | Filled with lots of friends | Warm and sunny all year
test: «The hostile dog growled at everyone who came near.» What does hostile mean here? | Friendly and playful | Tired and sleepy | *Unfriendly and angry | Quick and clever
test: «The climbers struggled in the hostile snowstorm.» What does hostile mean here? | Covered in bright colour | *Very harsh and difficult | Calm and gentle | Quick and easy
exam: Which meaning of hostile fits «hostile army»? | Very old and ancient | Sweet and tasty | *Belonging to an enemy | Giving out light and glowing
